<title>USA: Arrow Electronics sets $400 mln in debt.</title>
<headline>Arrow Electronics sets $400 mln in debt.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-01-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following two-part debt issue from Arrow Electronics was priced Thursday via Morgan Stanley &amp; Co, according to a source close to the deal.</p>
<p>BORROWER ARROW ELECTRONICS</p>
<p>AMT $200 MLN	 COUPON 7.00	 MATURITY 01/15/07</p>
<p>TYPE NOTES	   ISS PRICE 99.397  FIRST PAY DATE</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S A2    YIELD  7.085	PAY FREQ</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P     A     SPREAD 51 BPS     CALLABLE NO</p>
<p>AMT $200 MLN	 COUPON 7.50	 MATURITY 01/15/27</p>
<p>TYPE BONDS	   ISS PRICE 98.776  FIRST PAY DATE</p>
<p>LAST MOODY'S A2    YIELD  7.604	PAY FREQ</p>
<p>LAST S&amp;P     A     SPREAD 72 BPS     CALLABLE NO</p>
<p>U.S. corporate bond unit, 212 859-1675</p>
</text>
